"Hanford Hotel & Resort Uluwatu, Bali",Tropical Luxury in Harmony with Nature,"Jl. Goa Lempeh, Banjar Dinas Kangin, Uluwatu 80364, Bali, Indonesia",Indonesia,Asia-Pacific,Live,"<div><h1>Hanford Hotel & Resort Uluwatu Bali</h1> <h4><em><strong>Bali&rsquo;s hidden clifftop resort</strong></em></h4> </div> <div data-maxchar=""250""> <p>The Indian Ocean beckons from Hanford Hotel and Resort Uluwatu Bali. As you stand on the clifftop nearly 500 feet above sea level on the very southern tip of the Indonesian island, spectacular views spread out before you.</p> <p>The resort seamlessly blends two worlds &mdash; its 59 villas and five mansions feature sophisticated custom Italian furnishings by Milan-based architectural/design firm Antonio Citterio-Patricia Viel and Partners complemented by traditional Balinese design elements found throughout the property.&nbsp;</p> <p>As you take the buggy ride down the Italian cobblestone path to your frangipani-scented accommodations, you&rsquo;ll notice many features from the local volcanic landscape amid the lush tropical gardens.<a>.&nbsp;</a></p> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard01""><strong>Highlights</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>Be sure to visit the two Hanford stores onsite. One spotlights beautiful watches, fine jewelry and a wide selection of fragrances, while the other shop offers an inspired selection of wooden statues and cultural art pieces.</li> <li>Pampering is taken to another level at the oceanfront Hanford Spa. Be sure to check out the exclusive Hanford Signature Experiences &mdash; one designed for couples involves four highly trained therapists who provide a harmonious synchronized body massage.</li> <li>Want to go to the beach? Hop a ride on the inclinator, an open-sided carriage that leisurely carries you down the cliff to the resort&rsquo;s private stretch of sand and provides stunning views of the surrounding jungle.</li> <li>Take advantage of your surroundings and visit one of Bali&rsquo;s iconic religious monuments, Pura Luhur Uluwatu, which is only a 10-minute trek from the resort.</li> <li>History is everywhere at this Indonesian resort, where an antique Javanese Joglo house serves as the main entrance to the spa.</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard02""><strong>Things to Know</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>If you are feeling romantic, the onsite chapel features Paras Kerobokan stone from Bali and handcrafted floor-to-ceiling windows overlooking the endless blue ocean.</li> <li>Nearly two miles of white sand awaits you for relaxation, running, or long beach walks.</li> <li>For your convenience, a raised beachfront platform has been cleverly designed so that you can enjoy your time by the water during both low and high tide.</li> <li>If you are afraid of heights, sit on the little wooden seat at the back of the inclinator rather than gazing out from the glass front elevator.</li> <li>The resort offers a serene environment with world-class facilities and seamless access to Uluwatu's dramatic coastal scenery.</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard03""><strong>The Rooms</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>There are five villa accommodation categories from which to choose. Each of the 59 luxurious spaces has a private infinity pool and a beautiful tropical garden.</li> <li>The lavishly appointed villas have huge designer-made beds and either a comfortable couch or two loveseats for taking in the amazing ocean vistas.</li> <li>Five multi-level mansions offer a choice of three or five bedrooms with a maximum sleeping capacity of 12 people.</li> <li>The luxurious mansions feature fully equipped Miele high-end kitchens, landscaped wrap-around gardens, private two-tier swimming pools with sun decks, and regal interiors.</li> <li>For total privacy, consider the two-bedroom Hanford Villa, outfitted with indoor and outdoor living space and an ocean-facing swimming pool with sweeping views of the Indian Ocean.</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard04""><strong>The Restaurants</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>Il Ristorante – Niko Romito offers a unique tasting menu of Italian cuisine, influenced by seasonal Balinese ingredients and flavors, from a stunning location atop Uluwatu’s dramatic limestone cliffs.</li> <li>The range of fish on the menu at Il Ristorante changes in accordance with the seasons, which you can pair with one of the 200 wines on offer.</li> <li>Sangkar Restaurant is for more casual dining, with authentic Balinese dishes and classic Indonesian fare such as tender pork ribs wrapped in banana leaf or succulent scallop dishes.</li> <li>Casual cliffside dining at La Spiaggia focuses on classic, locally caught seafood, with fresh barramundi and lobster served with spicy Balinese sambal matah.</li> <li>Multiple dining venues ensure a rich blend of international and local flavors across the property.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> <div> <div> </div> </div> </div>","Bar, Beachfront platform, Cliffside inclinator, Gym, Meeting rooms, Oceanfront spa, Onsite boutique shops, Outdoor pool, Private beach, Private infinity pool, Restaurants, Wedding chapel",299,449,"2,499","1,999",129,"2,499",39,https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WlsykvMjpKvx52KZwspPMh0yG3mITesx/view?usp=drive_link,"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10iQMF5kCyYRRC3t9K7oe9GTUu3SOpFjP/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/10zhNCdxS4n5p6VpjfgjqAFW_SE4ESsB6/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/16Iy49hMvZADFbG6veDUto6gP_S99mfn6/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/17KY2_BELGFmlTmEruSEnSNQDWXm7uvRt/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/18LOIkJQqc17TgQGbrNQ8DW_HwXx72q_-/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/18MscLdT4MB2Iu0jAA4DDCNJAJkJOd-zA/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/18UWXSlrhzEUWqhxuZWABdCmTKKlJqdjp/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/19XCRs4r9wK2Zo1VFcQpv8bfiGL2BbY7k/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BIbYwW8um7WP6u878