Hanford Hotel & Resort Lago di Como,An Escape into Italian Lakeside Luxury,"Via Regina 40, 22012 Cernobbio, Lake Como, Italy",Italy,Europe,Live,"<div><h1>Hanford Hotel & Resort Lago di Como</h1> <h4><em><strong>A crown jewel of Lake Como</strong></em></h4> </div> <div data-maxchar=""250""> <p>Tucked away in a natural, private cove on Lake Como, Hanford Hotel & Resort Lago di Como embraces the vibrant scenery and the calm, cool waters that have been so suitably dubbed “the looking glass of Venus.”</p> <p>Originally built in the 16th century as a summer residence, the grand property features lavish foyers and 152 rooms adorned with classic artwork and antiquities.&nbsp;</p> <p>Privacy and discretion are of utmost importance at this luxury waterfront retreat, where guests can stroll through historic gardens or sunbathe by the stunning pool that floats in the midst of Lake Como.<a>.&nbsp;</a></p> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard01""><strong>Highlights</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>The resort’s 25-acre imperial garden and unique mosaic wall are signature icons that offer a timeless, historic atmosphere for guests to explore.</li> <li>Art lovers can enjoy guided tours to admire the paintings, sculptures, and antiques collected over the centuries, including historic frescoed ceilings.</li> <li>After a morning of sailing or tennis, guests can unwind with a Hydrasilk facial and Mud Mask body treatment at the Hanford Beauty Center.</li> <li>All accommodations open to views of Lake Como or the manicured gardens, featuring spacious walk-in closets and luxury marble-laid bathrooms.</li> <li>Making the most of its prime Lake Como location, almost all dining venues offer alfresco seating with vistas of the gorgeous gardens and sparkling waters.</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard02""><strong>Things to Know</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>The resort undergoes seasonal closure from mid-November to early March for annual upkeep and property maintenance.</li> <li>Guests can arrive in ultimate luxury via helicopter or yacht using the hotel's private helipad or marina facilities.</li> <li>Interactive culinary experiences are available, including private tours of the property's vegetable garden and seasonal cooking demonstrations.</li> <li>Families are warmly welcomed with dedicated amenities, babysitting services, and a dedicated kid's splash pool area.</li> <li>In springtime, the jasmine-swathed columns of the terrace archways exude a beautiful fragrance throughout the entire property.</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard03""><strong>The Rooms</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>The 152 accommodations are spread between the main historic building and the Queen’s Pavilion, offering quiet and serene garden or lake views.</li> <li>While no two rooms are exactly alike, the décor is lavishly comfortable, featuring old-world touches like thick drapes, dark woods, and classic chandeliers.</li> <li>The flagship suite offers a sumptuous 1,162-square-foot space complete with a panoramic lake view and an equally majestic private terrace.</li> <li>Accommodations in the Queen’s Pavilion afford vast views of Lake Como and are set away from the main house for maximum serenity.</li> <li>There are also four private villas on the property, including a hidden secluded retreat nestled within the garden’s striking mosaic wall.</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard04""><strong>The Restaurants</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>The culinary team transforms traditional regional recipes into gourmet meals, using fresh local fish and regional ingredients.</li> <li>Dining options range from casual evening venues like the Grill to the main restaurant, which serves breakfast, lunch, and dinner.</li> <li>A formal dress code is observed in the main dining rooms during evening service, with sought-after tables overlooking both the lake and garden.</li> <li>The poolside Sundeck provides alfresco drinks, while the main bar offers morning coffee, afternoon tea, and evening aperitifs in opulent surroundings.</li> <li>Multiple dining spaces provide seamless outdoor seating options to take full advantage of Lake Como's scenic backdrop.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> <div> <div> </div> </div> </div>","Babysitting services, Bar, Cooking demonstrations, Floating pool on Lake Como, Gym, Indoor pool, Kids pool, Meeting rooms, Outdoor pool, Poolside Sundeck, Private helipad, Private marina, Restaurants, Tennis, UNESCO-listed imperial garden, Villa d’Este Beauty Center",649,849,"4,999","3,999",279,"4,999",129,https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Fb1B3ainiSYYwRpkhAKIGVs_U6BIuAYI/view?usp=drive_link,"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1N9VvF_k0ZcbGXBdwRheGjKvcvv1Er2Zy/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1o9P706rwZkQI8MWTWC1URorE6sYT4wkU/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Ygc1ph2vPoSUf-zzAThx6MXNjvudn-7L/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xAAsjdFptvOOIxrp8b5MeG9PJTpNFVPJ/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1f06b6NGZJ8BP-3muYRuxfAkC6k6hWMj1/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KAWuLDhphFesQeJxEjiQrxRHpENUbJ6m/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MifcMdCvN0lSmDZqztmSsVVyaFU3npx5/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/18XVvHTJm6qI5fniuMzsTRkYoOViw8_PU/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/142zmFiXgzTA2Q6yK7_V6PbM7pIks2svA/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fZZYOv3HhzcrlYXxvm-PSl66nmrzDMK7/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/12N5a1KQB215cXwwhhLSxghbD-QqE3FXU/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1X1LynopMCzAJa741nPbrKAYC7VlRJnSL/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1iMu2tvKncEhWoPasBK5gh-GzWm2ixGLH/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VKfFnt7b-4FbjE6YLralNDymN3JCkgnj/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/10i4Xn797rsYuBRIG68Ps6wk05HhhX7mS/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/12XkKJ-EYpP7NaN