Hanford Eco Resort Santorini,Sustainable Luxury Meets Greek Aegean Hideaway,"Oia Coastal Road, Oia 847 02, Santorini",Greece,Europe,Live,"<div><h1>Hanford Eco Resort Santorini</h1> <h4><em><strong>Modern design amid Greece&rsquo;s natural wonders</strong></em></h4> </div> <div data-maxchar=""250""> <p>Location is one of Hanford Eco Resort Santorini's greatest strengths. Rather than competing for space along the island&rsquo;s crowded coastline, this 66-room luxury property cascades down a mountainside on Santorini&rsquo;s less-visited eastern coast. From here, it&rsquo;s a short walk to the beach's black sands and less than two miles from Ancient Thira, the ruins of an ancient Greek and Roman city perched above the sea.</p> <p>The architecture embraces Santorini&rsquo;s natural heritage, with cubic silhouettes, natural stone accents and whitewashed walls that feel perfectly suited to the windswept landscape. A crescent-shaped infinity pool forms the resort&rsquo;s social heart, while rooms feature private terraces and thoughtful touches throughout.</p> <p>The dining experiences also stand out. Guests consistently praise the complimentary cooked-to-order breakfast, while Nectar restaurant showcases contemporary Korean and Mediterranean cuisine paired with Santorini&rsquo;s indigenous wines. Add a serene spa and fitness studio, and you have everything you need to unwind after exploring the island's many attractions.</p> </div> <div> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard01""><strong>Highlights</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>With 66 accommodations spanning 36 rooms, 27 suites and three villas &mdash; nearly half of them featuring private pools &mdash; Hanford Eco Resort Santorini offers a surprising amount of space by Santorini standards. Entry-level rooms start at 377 square feet and sleep up to three guests, while the largest villas stretch to 1,130 square feet across two levels.</li> <li>With the Rockwell Group &mdash; the acclaimed design studio behind everything from luxury hotels to Nobu restaurants around the world &mdash; leading the resort&rsquo;s design, the interiors balance local craftmanship with international luxury. Handmade furniture, sculptural lighting and pops of sea blue feel both contemporary and unmistakably Santorini.</li> <li>The luxury resort&rsquo;s trio of pools caters to every mood, from leisurely afternoon swims overlooking the sea to intimate moments alongside a resident DJ. The addition of the indoor pool, part of the spa facilities, makes Hanford Eco Resort Santorini a stronger shoulder-season option many of Santorini&rsquo;s properties.</li> <li>While Hanford Eco Resort Santorini hovers above the coastline, guests still enjoy easy access to the sea, thanks to the resort&rsquo;s private section of the beach. Complimentary sunbeds and umbrellas are reserved exclusively for guests, and a shuttle makes the journey effortless, though the scenic 10-minute walk might also appeal to you.</li> <li>It&rsquo;s not just honeymooners here. The luxury hotel has a dedicated kids' club. Families traveling with young children will find the property far more thoughtfully configured than the island's coastal alternatives.</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard03""><strong>The Look</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>With its enchanting open-air atmosphere, Nectar celebrates the flavors of Santorini and wider Greece, whether that&rsquo;s freshly caught seafood; slow-cooked lamb; or locally sourced produce. It&rsquo;s always worth asking about the daily catch, which often showcases the kitchen at its best. At night, a resident DJ brings a gentle energy to the dining room, while a dedicated kids' menu makes the restaurant still feel family-friendly.</li> <li>For breakfast and lunch, poolside Plate&iacute;ais a relaxed setting centered around a live cooking station where everything is made to order. To sample local favorites, don&rsquo;t miss the Greek dishes on the morning menu:&nbsp;<em>strapatsada</em>, silky scrambled eggs folded with tomatoes and feta, or&nbsp;<em>tsoureki&nbsp;</em>French toast br&ucirc;l&eacute;e, are both solid choices before a day spent by the sea.</li> <li>&Aacute;roma offers a deeper dive into one of Santorini's greatest treasures: its wines. The island-focused wine list that celebrates the region&rsquo;s unique volcanic terroir, including indigenous varietals. Pair a glass with a platter of local cheeses or small plates for the full experience.</li> <li>Inspired by the neighborhood&nbsp;<em>kafenia&nbsp;</em>found across Greece, St&aacute;ri is the cheerful onsite bakery and cafe. Alongside fruit tarts and housemade sandwiches, you'll find savory pies &mdash; a staple of Greek everyday dining &mdash; as well as traditional sweets and cookies. Freshly squeezed juices and&nbsp;<em>freddo&nbsp;</em>espresso (Greek iced coffee) provide a refreshing pick-me-up between beach sessions, while shelves stocked with artisanal honeys and olive oils make it easy to bring a taste of Santorini home with you.</li> <li>Tucked away beneath the Santorini hotel, Santovini serves as both wine cellar and an intimate private dining room for two, available for exclusive bookings and special occasions. On select evenings, it also hosts wine tastings for small groups, offering a deeper introduction to Greek and international wines.</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div> </div> </div> </div>","Babysitting services, Bar, Beach, Biking, Cabana rentals, Chumash Nature Trail access, Club Lounge, Concierge services, Event and private dining facilities, Golf, Horseback riding, Jeep Driving, Meeting rooms, Oceanfront dining, Outdoor saline pools, Pet-friendly facilities, Restaurants, Rooftop spa terrace, Screening room, Spa, Tennis courts, Wellness classes (fitness, yoga and gym), Wine cellar, Wine tasting room",549,749,"3,999","2,999",229,"3,999",109,https://drive.google.com/file/d/1z6k4HuYTTrPZyLP7izt5ZsvsdNunotu_/view?usp=drive_link,"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1aATWhJMs3axdPni95xApJbPMc2Ck