Hanford Grand Hotel Vancouver,Timeless Elegance on Canada’s Pacific Coast,"1055 Canada Place, Vancouver, BC V6C 0C3",Canada,North America,Live,"<div><h1>Hanford Grand Hotel Vancouver</h1> <h4><em><strong>Sleek Pacific Rim style in Vancouver</strong></em></h4> </div> <div data-maxchar=""250""> <p>The Hanford Grand Hotel Vancouver mixes Asian and west coast elements, offering an extensive art program, plenty of high-tech amenities and several stylish restaurants and lounges that attract both travelers and locals.</p> <p>At the hotel’s main entrance, a grove of sparkling trees lights the way into the lobby where you'll find several vivid street-scene photographs captured by Vancouver artist Fred Herzog, serving as a vivid reminder that you're in a vibrant city with an impressive cultural scene.&nbsp;</p> <p>Located one block from the Coal Harbour waterfront, it provides an ideal base for exploring downtown business destinations, local arts, and nearby natural wonders.<a>.&nbsp;</a></p> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard01""><strong>Highlights</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>The hotel’s wide-ranging art collection begins on the exterior, with a unique text installation wrapping the building's facades, alongside a featured $225,000 white handcrafted Fazioli piano in the lobby lounge.</li> <li>Bicycles are provided for guests, complete with bike butlers in the summer to offer cycling maps for exploring Stanley Park, Vancouver’s massive urban rainforest located just a short ride away.</li> <li>Select corner rooms feature deep Japanese ofuro soaking tubs with two walls of windows overlooking seaplanes taking off on Burrard Inlet and the lush rooftop gardens nearby.</li> <li>On the sixth-floor terrace, a heated pool and hot tub are open year-round with five private cabanas available to rent, accompanied by a poolside cabana bar serving drinks from May through October.</li> <li>Opt for Hanford Gold category rooms for exclusive access to a private 20th-floor lounge with spectacular views of Stanley Park, the water, and the North Shore mountains.</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard02""><strong>Things to Know</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>To get around town, the Coal Harbour hotel offers a complimentary house car service using comfortable Cadillac vehicles, including fully electric models.</li> <li>Hanford Grand Hotel Vancouver is conveniently situated one block from the Vancouver Convention Centre, within easy walking distance of the Gastown and West End neighborhoods.</li> <li>The fifth floor features a newly renovated Hanford Spa with 14 treatment rooms, a vast outdoor terrace with two hot tubs, an infrared sauna, and a state-of-the-art 24-hour Wellness Club.</li> <li>Guest rooms occupy floors six to 22 of the 45-story tower, while the upper levels feature private residential condominiums.</li> <li>The advanced Wellness Club provides high-end cardio and strength equipment, recovery tools, a Pilates reformer, and personalized fitness experiences with expert trainers.</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard03""><strong>The Rooms</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>The 367 guest rooms and 47 suites are sleek and modern, featuring warm American walnut paneling, backlit photos of Pacific Northwest rainforests, and crisp white linens with cream accents.</li> <li>In-room technology includes built-in media panels, electronic controls for lighting and window shades, and tablets loaded with a virtual concierge to order room service or request valet car retrieval.</li> <li>Rooms come equipped with Nespresso coffee makers and mini-bars stocked with locally made snacks for your convenience.</li> <li>The spa-like marble bathrooms are fitted with premium Le Labo bath products and a small flat-screen television cleverly built directly into the vanity mirror.</li> <li>Spacious layouts offer quiet luxury designed to blend high-tech convenience with the relaxed beauty of the surrounding Vancouver landscape.</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard04""><strong>The Restaurants</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>The airy Lobby Lounge features marble floors, a 20-foot fireplace, craft cocktails, and daily live music performances surrounding its centerpiece white Fazioli piano.</li> <li>Tucked into the lobby, the Raw Bar serves sustainable seafood from local waters and across the Pacific, perfectly paired with an curated selection of sake.</li> <li>Botanist restaurant celebrates the abundant bounty of British Columbia, utilizing regional produce, sustainably sourced seafood, and organic ingredients across four botanical-inspired spaces.</li> <li>Guests can experience distinct atmospheres within Botanist, including a vibrant bar, a lush indoor garden, a main dining room, and a cozy Taschen Library.</li> <li>In-room dining is also available with 24-hour room service offering selections from the hotel's acclaimed culinary teams.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> <div> <div> </div> </div> </div>","Babysitting services, Bar, Bicycles, Fairmont Gold private lounge, Hot tubs, House car service, Infrared sauna, Meeting rooms, Outdoor heated pool, Pilates reformer, Poolside cabana bar, Restaurants, Spa, Wellness club",449,599,"2,999",,189,"3,499",139,https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RjDZ0vxp35h9WUcgyDmJszJ0mJy_mwzZ/view?usp=drive_link ,"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1z7CE8tvlHZVB_Aa01fs4dX2bEuonydvi/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RjDZ0vxp35h9WUcgyDmJszJ0mJy_mwzZ/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UCK8iVPo1rUc3xzQCM0YaYdV0GwbJ8_J/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hT847aCUQgq4jsHX-LcNAeiwi6DP5vj3/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VE_khDcezK7yU9q_ni_ZiuDE6mdUQLW5/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sWv3avCzeAAJ2CFew7o3UVLgioFVTape/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Y1C6aQCMlsU4jL_yc67j4mwW1jGrg9Bg/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/12NceSH9J6bPOKCrpkhw_QBaJNfxT6T5C/view?usp=dr