Hanford Eco Resort Jeju,A Coastal Sanctuary Inspired by Jeju’s Natural Beauty,"152 Taepyeong-ro, Seogwipo-si, Jeju-do 63571",South Korea,Asia-Pacific,Live,"<div><h1>Hanford Eco Resort Jeju</h1> <h4><em><strong>Modern design amid Korea&rsquo;s natural wonders</strong></em></h4> </div> <div data-maxchar=""250""> <p>A vision of contemporary Korean luxury, Hanford Eco Resort Jeju stretches across the southern cliffs of Jeju, offering a back-to-nature experience on South Korea&rsquo;s famed volcanic island.</p> <p>With its clean architectural lines and sun-drenched gardens, the low-lying resort blends seamlessly into the dramatic landscape. Inside, renowned interior designer Bill Bensley worked his magic to unveil a&nbsp;<em>hanok</em>-inspired lobby and relaxing rooms featuring sunny hues, light wood and natural stone.&nbsp;</p> <p>From world-class wellness to family fun, do as much &mdash; or a little &mdash; as you please. Indulge in an organic treatment at the Hanford Spa, take a dip in the expansive infinity pool and practice sun salutations with views of the East China Sea<a>.&nbsp;</a>When hunger strikes, savor wood-fired barbecue at The Flying Hog or lavish brunches at Island Kitchen.</p> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard01""><strong>Highlights</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>Jeju is a UNESCO Biosphere Reserve and World Natural Heritage Site, so it&rsquo;s no surprise that Hanford Eco Resort Jeju celebrates nature at every opportunity. You&rsquo;ll sense it everywhere &mdash; in the breezy clifftop setting, lush gardens, fresh local ingredients and in the interior design, where floor-to-ceiling windows keep the stunning landscape at top of mind.</li> <li>Spacious accommodations, starting at 463 square feet, also honor Jeju&rsquo;s spirit with bursts of yellow and bathrooms designed to feel like mini&nbsp;<em>jjimjilbang</em>&nbsp;(Korean bathhouses), complete with gigantic marble soaking tubs. Most rooms offer sea views, though ground-floor accommodations swap views for a garden terrace and a circular, cypress-wood tub.</li> <li>The stone-clad Hanford Spa has it all: relaxation lounges, an indoor lap pool, sunken Jacuzzi, fitness center, yoga studio and access to a natural hot spring complex. Meanwhile, the facials and sea-inspired body treatments feature premium natural and organic products from the likes of Elemis and Thermes Marins de Saint-Malo.</li> <li>With its energetic open kitchen, flavorful wood-fired dishes and ocean views, The Flying Hog is perfect for a date night or memorable family dinner. For a quieter evening, reserve seats at Yeoumul for an omakase experience showcasing ultra-fresh local seafood.</li> <li>Soak up the Jeju sun at the resort&rsquo;s outdoor infinity pool, which seems to flow into the sea. If a stroll through the countryside is more your speed, set out on the Jeju Olle Trail Route 7 cliffside walking trail to explore charming fishing villages and lush farmlands.</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard03""><strong>The Look</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>Designed by the internationally acclaimed architecture firm WATG, this clifftop retreat draws inspiration from Korea&rsquo;s traditional Choga architecture &mdash; thatched-roof homes known as&nbsp;<em>hanok</em><a>.&nbsp;</a>Offering a modern take, the architects incorporated sleek stone, straight lines and carefully placed voids, allowing sea breezes and sunlight to flow seamlessly throughout the space.</li> <li>Bill Bensley-designed interiors allow Jeju&rsquo;s natural beauty and culture to shine. In the guest rooms, pale wood and pops of yellow reflect the island&rsquo;s vibrant fields of canola flowers, while muted grey, black and white tones reference Jeju&rsquo;s volcanic terrain.</li> <li>In another nod to the island&rsquo;s roots, the resort&rsquo;s villas feature traditional Jeju roof tiles that add a touch of authenticity to the otherwise contemporary design.</li> <li>Organic textures and materials, such as reclaimed wood accents and woven rattanfurnishings in the guest rooms and common areas evoke a sense of warmth and tranquility.</li> <li>Take some time to explore Hanford Eco Resort Jeju&rsquo;s contemporary art collection. Works by renowned artists like Jeff Koons and Damien Hirst are paired with pieces from Korean talent like Kim Tschang-Yeul.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> <div> <div> </div> </div> </div>","Bar, Family-friendly facilities, Fitness classes, Garden terraces, Gym, Indoor lap pool, Jacuzzi, Natural hot spring, Organic spa treatments, Outdoor infinity pool, Pilates classes, Recreational facilities, Relaxation lounges, Restaurants, Spacious accommodations, Yoga studio",349,349,"1,999","2,999",129,"1,799",59,https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mPb0Q1aRCfCyqdGILqSrjHqFV-TQi9qZ/view?usp=drive_link,"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1mPb0Q1aRCfCyqdGILqSrjHqFV-TQi9qZ/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1HdsR0fzG9bcTJ3_xQS9iftF4oTLtxWsR/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NmGAwtjLy7IUV4YSdsZTHIkfEXWCX88n/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Myk0eBwu4mSrrETYd_qtf75o3HtzR883/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1t77gR3Ted5FSaS7YrEaeF2CQR349Xr_w/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hAMW2v4f-AZh3UGMXD5MoD8mOXJEqjKo/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/100_izhGPvadQkeOlEtyPKydXVHW8C3s3/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1syS3MxG97LOgQadkWti7nXrdRz2zY8NZ/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/14eMJS0-jdxs76DeaX8Afuerr7ZhM1Vu1/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PCdpQ0F0NpWPC1jgl25Xbd6XIhRC351P/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WFpX-AwffuFz2UGpYAA65EX8on_B-UCo/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/11aPBKpYuhJqUlI7ItFPvAyP_jUjtVAZH/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/15ZG4xTz4mAbPxmdt8GzNJsEion3-imPC/view?usp=drive_link, https://drive.google.com/file/d/1YkOgiYp4bLdr50em55w9eyhGqcdUz1vw/view?u