Hanford Grand Hotel Melbourne,Contemporary Luxury with a European Soul,"1 Parliament Place, East Melbourne VIC 3002",Australia,Asia-Pacific,Live,"<div><h1>Hanford Grand Hotel Melbourne</h1> <h4><em><strong>Sky-high luxury at Australia&rsquo;s tallest hotel</strong></em></h4> </div> <div data-maxchar=""250""> <p>Towering more than 60 stories above the city skyline, Hanford Grand Hotel Melbourne occupies the top 17 floors of the 80-story West Side Place Tower, offering unmatched 360-degree panoramas across Victoria&rsquo;s vibrant cultural capital.</p> <p>Designed with gallery-like interiors, sleek furniture, neutral tones, and endless walls of floor-to-ceiling windows, the property celebrates abundant natural light and Melbourne&rsquo;s rich artistic heritage.&nbsp;</p> <p>From sunset dips in the 64th-floor heated infinity pool to vintage cocktails on the 80th floor, every detail elevates urban hospitality above the clouds.<a>.&nbsp;</a></p> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard01""><strong>Highlights</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>Taking up the top 17 floors of an 80-story tower, the hotel offers unmatched 360-degree views of Melbourne&rsquo;s skyline and Port Phillip Bay.</li> <li>Take a sunset dip in the 64th-floor heated indoor infinity pool, framed by double-height windows with geometric metal detailing and plush daybeds.</li> <li>Sip sundowners at the cozy 80th-floor Cameo lounge, specializing in vintage pours and classic cocktails crafted with rare antique spirits.</li> <li>The Level 64 spa sanctuary features vitality pools, saunas, steam rooms, and holistic treatments using locally sourced botanicals and premium skincare.</li> <li>Thoughtful artistic touches include bronze lobby door handles cast by Indigenous artist Maree Clarke and a historic black marble water feature outside the spa.</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div> <h3 data-target=""#ard02""><strong>Things to Know</strong></h3> <div> <ul> <li>An express elevator whisks guests directly to the 80th-floor sky lobby for 